{
  "probe": "agent-lanes preset — subagent tool-surface own-layer leak and grandchild escalation (behavioral smoke 2026-09-13)",
  "capturedAt": "2026-09-13T09:14:08.379Z",
  "howToReproduce": "In an agent-lanes session in this workspace, delegate one oracle and let it call the generic subagent tool once; then run: node scripts/verify-agent-lanes.cjs --all. The depth-2 grandchildren surface as \"跳过（非 agent-lanes 子代理）\". Per-session fields come from: zstd -dc ~/.dsh/sessions/<slug>/<id>/session.v3.jsonl.zstd",
  "environment": {
    "preset": "agent-lanes",
    "workspace": "/Users/eric/Project/tests/dsh-plugins/cireric-dsh-agent-lanes"
  },
  "findings": [
    "A delegated child sees toolFilter whitelist + subagent + list_subagent_models. The extra pair is this file subject.",
    "Cause: the preset tool-subagent row sets modelSelectionSettings: true, so tool-subagent takes the standing scoped install path (packages/subagent/tool-subagent/src/index.ts:663-680) and registers those two tools (list-models at :362) into EVERY composition member own scope layer.",
    "Own-layer registrations are inserted after the masking loop (core/tools/src/index.ts:1166-1172), so toolFilter.allow cannot mask them. deny and plugin-side mounting are equally ineffective.",
    "subagent_fork does NOT take that path; it exists only on the inherited surface, so it IS masked correctly — verifiable here: it is absent from every child tool list.",
    "Consequence: oracle (depth 1, whitelist read/grep/glob/lsp/explorer/librarian) used the leaked subagent tool to spawn three depth-2 grandchildren, each with 162 tools, no role persona, and the orchestrator persona.",
    "Mitigation: agent.cordis.yml tool-subagent row gained maxDepth: 1 (2026-09-13); a depth-1 role re-delegating computes childDepth 2 > 1 and throws SubagentDepthError."
  ],
